# Lesson 2, based on the Lesson 2 bidding exercise 4a (partner opens 1NT), reworked to 9 HCP so 3NT makes on plain play.
title: Partner opens 1NT: invite with 8
id: L02-05
type: exercise
lesson: 2
concepts: 2.4, 2.7
student: S
board: 5
dealer: N
vulnerable: NS

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  A85    KQ5    AKJ72  92
  E  Q64    JT98   T53    AJ6
  S  K97    A743   Q6     T843
  W  JT32   62     984    KQ75

auction:
  N 1NT    = 15-17 points, balanced
  E Pass
  S 2NT*   = 8-9 points, balanced: an invitation
     key: 9 HCP and balanced. Raise to 2NT: partner will bid game with a maximum.
     not 3NT: 3NT shows 10+. Did you count 9?
     not Pass: Did you count 9? With 8-9 you can invite game.
     not *: With a balanced 9, which raise of 1NT invites game?
  W Pass
  N 3NT    = A maximum: accepts the invitation
  E Pass
  S Pass
  W Pass

auction recap:
  Your 2NT said: 8-9 points, balanced. If partner has 15 or 16, your side
  may be short of 25, so she passes. With 17 she knows there is enough,
  and bids game. North is declarer, because she bid no-trump first, and so
  East will lead to the first trick.

play:
  1   E HJ  S H3  W H2  N HQ
  2   N D2  E D3  S DQ  W D4
      note: Declarer's plan: take the diamonds, then the hearts and spades, before the defenders get in. Dummy's ♦Q goes first, the high card from the short side.
  3   S D6  W D8  N DA  E D5
      note: Back to declarer's diamonds.
  4   N DK  E DT  S C3  W D9
      note: Keep running the diamonds.
  5   N DJ  E S4  S C4  W H6
      note: Keep going.
  6   N D7  E S6  S C8  W C5
      note: The last diamond.
  7   N S5  E SQ  S SK  W S2
      note: Now a spade toward dummy's king.
  8   S S7  W ST  N SA  E C6
      note: Back to declarer's ♠A.
  9   N HK  E H8  S H4  W S3
      note: The heart winners.
  10  N H5  E H9  S HA  W C7
      note: A heart to dummy's ace.
  11  S CT  W CQ  N C2  E CA
      note: Ten tricks are in. Dummy leads a club, and the defenders take the rest.
  12  E CJ  S H7  W CK  N C9
  13  W SJ  N S8  E HT  S S9
      note: 10 tricks: 3NT made with an overtrick.

play recap:
  Declarer's plan: take the diamonds, then the hearts and spades, before
  the defenders get in.

  3NT made with an overtrick. Your side had 26 points. Your invitation let
  partner decide, because only she knew whether she had 15 or 17.
